    "sync_diagram.one_vm": "Single VM";
    "sync_diagram.part_1.label": "Part 1";
    "sync_diagram.part_1.text": "Every change to your data passes through a <strong>REST API</strong> (OpenAPI 3.1). Permissions are checked on every request. 3rd party services can use it. When the sync engine is down, your API still works.";
    "sync_diagram.part_2.label": "Part 2";
    "sync_diagram.part_2.text": "The <strong>CDC (Change Data Capture)</strong> worker subscribes to a WAL (Write-Ahead Log), processes the logs & stores activities in db, and sends changes back to the API → API sends an SSE to notify the client about a change → client then does a normal API request.";
    "sync_diagram.part_3.label": "Part 3";
    "sync_diagram.part_3.text": "For <strong>collaborative editing & online presence</strong>, the <strong>Yjs</strong> worker logs every edit as it arrives and relays it to clients. Permission is verified directly against the DB. A few seconds after the last edit, the worker hands the merged document to the API to save. Those not editing receive that write as an SSE notification.";
    "sync_diagram.part_4.label": "Part 4";
    "sync_diagram.part_4.text": "For small apps, <strong>one VM can run it all</strong>: the API process also starts the CDC, Yjs and other workers, with the frontend beside it. Nothing changes in how the parts talk to each other. One config flag gives each service its own VM.";
    "sync_diagram.toggle_labels": "Toggle all data-flow labels";
